course: dictionary
lesson: 9553
title: Storey and floors
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A storey is one floor or level of a building. The ground floor is the first level, and each floor above it is another storey.
explain: «Borneo is a huge island in Southeast Asia covered in some of the oldest rainforest on Earth, where trees grow taller than a thirty-storey building.» The clue is thirty-storey. It tells you the building has thirty floors stacked on top of each other, so the trees are taller than that.
explain: When storey joins another word, look at the front part first. «Multi-storey» means many floors, so a multi-storey car park has lots of levels for cars. A two-storey house has two floors.
fact: A storey is one floor or level of a building.
fact: «Multi-storey» describes a building with many floors, like a multi-storey car park.
fact: «A two-storey house» has two floors.
fact: «On the top storey» means on the highest floor of a building.
fact: Storey is spelt s-t-o-r-e-y. Do not mix it up with story, which means a tale.
exercise: How many floors does «a two-storey house» have? | Thirty | *Two | One | Ten
exercise: What does «multi-storey» mean? | Very small | *Having many floors | Made of glass | Under the ground
exercise: In «the top storey», where are you? | *On the highest floor | Under the ground | At the front door
test: A giant is «three storeys tall». How tall is the giant? | As small as a mouse | *As tall as three floors stacked up | As wide as a road | Under one floor tall
test: Which building has many storeys? | A bungalow with one room | *A ten-storey block of flats | A shed in the garden | A tent on the grass
exam: What does «on the top storey» mean for a flat? | In the basement | In the middle of the road | On the ground floor | *On the highest floor
